      "problem": "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic paraboloid $z-1=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2} \\\\ z-1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} \\\\ z & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives us the equation of the parabola in $xz$-plane.",
